Z||000003||FieroLisa||12-27-2001||02:29 AM||||Those User-Errors are a real b*tch eh??<P>Honestly I'm a little bugged that you would choose to express your opinions in this way, but hey at least I can be glad that I am not a customer service  representative in Old Orchard Beach, Maine.<P>Anyway, whatever problems you were having, whether they were handset related (and that model is about 3 or 4 years old so that might be a clue) or billing, every cell phone company has it's equal problems. So go to Verizon or AT&T and get ready to be all frustrated at them, too. <BR><P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.webjolt.f2s.com/pictures/fierolisa.gif">                 <BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa" TARGET=_blank>FieroLisa's Website</A> *<A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa1/showdates.html" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Events 2002</A> *<A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/ncfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tarheel Fieros</A>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Indy-2M4||12-27-2001||06:29 AM||||Holy Crap!! That poor phone! However I feel like doing that to my stupid Motorola Startac that has stupid Verizon. It sucks...hell, I never had dropped calls with my Cinci Bell I Wireless phone. And if it wasnt for the year and a half that I have left on that stupid contract, I'd do the same to my phone. Anyone know what the price to pay is if you breach the Verizon Contract? Like I said, I have about a year and 5 months to go on it.<P>------------------<BR>Kathy<BR>http:\\sofa.iwarp.com<BR>    <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/IndyCrueSig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
