Z||000008||Fiero_24||12-27-2001||08:41 AM||||Sprint Sucks!!!!!  I had calls that were not mine, and so they gave me 1 free month to figure out where the calls where coming from.  I used 22 minutes and got a $725 bill in the mail.  My girlfriend had the same problem ($500 bill), and so did 2 of my neighbors.  I refuse to pay them, and I filed a complaint.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/driverside41.jpg"> <BR>  <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24</A> <BR>1987 GT||||reg||8
Z||000009||LarryB||12-27-2001||08:52 AM||||Lisa, you're probably right in that you wouldn't want to be a customer service rep for Sprint in the OOB area.  Sprint service in Maine is non-competitive.  You just happened to mention the 2 national companies that DO offer competitive service in Maine - Verizon & AT&T.  The issue isn't the pricing, but what you're actually getting for your money. <P>Sprint is my company's "preferred" choice in the US.  It's usually pretty good in larger cities but once you get outside the immediate metro area digital service is spotty, which is why all the long-haul techs I know don't use Sprint's service - Sprint charges high roaming fees per minute of analog use.  Which leads to this:  Sprint only offers analog service over the vast majority of the State of Maine.  You can readily confirm this for yourself; I know this is true because being a Maine native and landowner with family living throughout the state I spend a significant amount of time traveling there.<P>Sprint's digital service in Maine is limited to the cities and towns bordering I-95 on the 51-mile-long stretch from Kittery up to just north of Portland.  That's great if Tim is calling from around the corner from his house, but if he drives 10 miles inland and makes a call he's in for a nasty surprise on his next monthly statement.   <P>Verizon and AT&T both have digital coverage over a significant portion of the state and do not charge their customers roaming fees when operating in those remaining analog-only areas. <P>So - Verizon and AT&T Wireless customers in Maine may not get any better customer service, but at least the'll get better service coverage, including nationwide long distance if they want it. <P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroLisa:<BR><B>Those User-Errors are a real b*tch eh??<P>Honestly I'm a little bugged that you would choose to express your opinions in this way, but hey at least I can be glad that I am not a customer service  representative in Old Orchard Beach, Maine.<P>Anyway, whatever problems you were having, whether they were handset related (and that model is about 3 or 4 years old so that might be a clue) or billing, every cell phone company has it's equal problems. So go to Verizon or AT&T and get ready to be all frustrated at them, too. <P><BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||9
Z||000010||firstfiero||12-27-2001||08:57 AM||||         I'm an att customer and I got to admit I like it a hell of alot more when they were cellular one. any cell phone co will have problems but I must admit that all my friends that have sprint are constantly haveing billing problems!||||reg||1
Z||000011||Formula88||12-27-2001||09:28 AM||||Well, I've been an Alltell subscriber for about 5 or 6 years now.  Their customer service is ok, and the coverage area is again, just ok.  What I have learned is, that even if it's their top of the line phone, Motorola phones suck a$$!  I've got a Star Tac that's a bit over 1 year old, and it's already had the antennae replaced twice and the circuit borad inside once.  And it needs both again.<P>I'm looking for a better deal.  A friend of mine in the area has Sprint PCS and says he's quite happy with it.  That could be due to the different area.  I don't know.  He also has a nice Samsung phone I was looking to get, but Alltell didn't offer it.  Looks like it may be time to swap carriers...<P>Hey, Lisa, got any good deals on new UberPhones?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||11
