Z||000013||REDHOTT88||12-27-2001||10:54 AM||||Cell Phone service plans??<P>You mean how much money are you willing for us to SUCK out of you, and still get the same shitty service as the next guy...<P>We need to make more cool commercials that make life sound so great, "IF" you use one of our phone plans !!!<P>Phone companies could give two shits if you're actually happy.. "Just keep sending in the money and shut the hell up!!!"    <IMG SRC="http://www.stopstart.fsnet.co.uk/smilie/jpshakehead.gif">   <P>------------------<BR>                                                                                                         <BR>                 <IMG SRC="http://www.stopstart.fsnet.co.uk/smilie/FIREdevil.gif">       <FONT COLOR="ffoooo"> <B>1988 Formula 2.8L V6</B> 5 speed Getrag </FONT><BR>            <I><FONT SIZE="1">(Runs smooth, shifts crisp, goes fast, red and shiny all over!)</FONT></I><BR><p>[This message has been edited by REDHOTT88 (edited 12-27-2001).]||||reg||13
Z||000014||fierobaby||12-27-2001||11:17 AM||||I have cingular and love it I have not had problems yet and plus the phone was free!||||reg||1
Z||000015||CoolBlue87GT||12-27-2001||11:24 AM||||Gee, that's a pretty neat trick, how'd you keep from 'breaking ground'?  lol<P>I work for RadioShack, we sell both Sprint & Verison (used to sell Altel)<P>For starters, as someone already said, that Qualcom phone sucks.  It's almost the worst phone, The worst is the Motorla Startac.<P>Sizewise is fine, just does not have the power to "get out"<P>I have a Sprint PCS Sanyo 4000 phone.<P>The only reason I have it, is the plan offered to the employees. $15 a month, almost unlimited time & long distance free.<P>The Verison employee plan is not as good time wise.<P>Now, as far as service area, Verison is the sure winner there. More coverage area, Plus their phone are 'triband'<P>Which means analog & digital & PCS bands.<P>Where the PCS signal is the strongest, it use Sprint towers (at not charge) - with the correct plan in place.<P>Hands down in the S/W part of Florida where I live, Verison is the better choise. - Of course, in a big city, Sprint might be better.<P>So, tell me how'd you do that trick with the backhoe ?||||reg||1
Z||000016||summerjim||12-27-2001||11:26 AM||||I completely understand Tim's frustrations with Sprint PCS (that stands for Pretty Crappy Service).<P>I bought a Samsung SCH3500 (not cheap, and supposedly a good phone) from their website back in the summer of 2000. They took my credit card number when I ordered it, but sent me a bill in the mail also. Not having seen my credit card statement yet, I just paid the bill that came in the mail and assumed they took my credit card online for a security thing. NOPE! They DOUBLE BILLED me for the phone. Took SIX months for them to resolve it.  I was calling twice a week for 6 months before they fixed it. Got all different stories: they had no record of the charge, it would be fixed in 24 hours, it would be fixed within a week, we can't help you, our investiation is ongoing. You name it, I heard it. I sent them a copy of my cleared check AND credit card statement. They still played dumb. <P>A few months ago, my wonderful Samsung 3500 phone started acting flaky. Apparently a chaffed wire (it's a flip phone) going to the speaker. Made it hard to use the phone. (couldn't hear anyone) I called Sprint twice about it and was on hold for OVER TWO HOURS waiting for someone to answer. Then they were like, oh, it's beyond the 1 year warranty, we can't help you. Buy another phone or pay to have it fixed.<P>I've heard from LOTS of other people (and even on one of those radio consumer advocate shows) that this phone has problems with chaffing wires. Yet Sprint wouldn't do anything about it. Their customer service absolutely sucks.<P>As long as you're on the highway, you get good coverage. Drive 2 miles off the highway and you better plan on paying about $0.35 a minute because you're off their network.<P>Let's see... over 2 hours waiting to talk to someone, screwed up billing for over 6 months and a junk phone that they sold me and won't do anything about even though it's a known problem.<P>That's 3 strikes against SprintPCS in my book. <P>Hey Tim, maybe I'll bring my SprintPCS phone over and we can crush mine too!! (since it doesn't work right, I can't donate to the women's shelter). Get the camera ready.||||reg||1
Z||000017||LZeitgeist||12-27-2001||12:00 PM||||I'm with Alltel... got an Audiovox CDM-3300 dual-mode flip phone. <P>For $29.95/month, I get 200 (250?) free minutes per month, free long-distance anywhere in the US (originating from my home area), and no roaming charges anywhere. Also have voicemail, caller ID, call-forwarding, call-waiting, and all those goodies. For an extra $2.95/month, I also have damage insurance on the phone - it breaks, they fix/replace it.<P>It's a little chunkier than I was hoping to find, but it's a workhorse. It's been beat to heck - the case looks like hell - but it still works great. <P>I had an Ericsson before this one... they can kiss my lily-white butt. The new one I started the contract with worked fine for 11-1/2 months on a 12-month contract, then crapped out. Under warranty, they state that they reserve the right to choose to replace it with either a new or a refurbished one. I got a refurbished one in exchange. It lasted a month. I got another refurbished one in exchange - it lasted a month. Did this <B>5 times</B>, and they still refused to send me a brand-new phone. I finally smashed the damn thing with a cinderblock and mailed it back to them, told them to keep it, and that they could kiss my a** - I would *never* use or recommend Ericsson products again.<P>------------------<BR>Patrick W. Heinske  --  LZeitgeist@aol.com<BR>1988 Red Fiero Formula<BR>- 1st Place - Stock Coupe - FOCOSEVA 2000<BR>- 3rd Place - Stock Formula - FOCOA Nat'l 2001<BR>- Class Winner - 1982 to Present - Tarheel Tigers All-Pontiac Show 2001||||reg||1
Z||000018||SLAMMED87GT||12-27-2001||06:34 PM||||Well- I got a brand new Samsung h105 and it just kicks ass! Has internet, e-mail, messaging, games, free nationwide longdistance, no roaming charges, and has great sound quality! I am going through voicestream and they have been good as of yet! <P>I got a pretty good deal as the store I bought it from advertise with us!<P>------------------<BR>3" Drop, 17" Primax 618s/Nitto450 205/40, 4" Monza exhaust, Mudstain decklid scoop, 7" wing stands, Clear front and rear lights, custom interior, all options...that's all hehe.||||reg||6
Z||000019||Master_Sushi||12-27-2001||07:48 PM||||Verizon is really the only good cell phone service where I live. I use to have a Sprint, and I just recently got rid of a Cingular, they both were rips offs. I go to Canada allot (every weekend) and I have a plan that covers all of the US and Canada in one local area. I forget how much extra a month it is, like 10$ or something. But its worth it for me. My cingular didn't even work at my house   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif">... With Verizon I get full digital almost everywhere.<P>Oh ya my Nokia 5185i has been great so far. I had an old erickson b4 that , it sucked...<p>[This message has been edited by Master_Sushi (edited 12-27-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000020||mrfiero||12-27-2001||07:56 PM||||That has got to be the funniest thing I have seen in a long time!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I use Sprint PCS here in the Denver area and for the most part it's OK.  I do get a few dropped calls every once in a while and one day I lost service for 3 hours.  Oh well.<P>I'm committed for at least 11 more months, so hopefully my phone doesn't go on the fritz (same model as summerjims). <BR>||||reg||10
Z||000021||fieroparts.com||12-27-2001||08:19 PM||||QUOTE]Originally posted by CoolBlue87GT:<BR><B><P>So, tell me how'd you do that trick with the backhoe ?</B>[/QUOTE]<P>No tricks, I just know how to run my back hoe<BR>loader. I have smashed Fieros with it, rolled<BR>them over, ripped the roofs off them (after all of the good parts are taken off.<P><BR>Sprint sucks!  I have a tower less then 3/10ths. of a mile from my house (yes, sprint has service on it) and it still sucked.<P>I had no problems with the phone I ripped into 162 small pieces, it was 99% all service.<P>I too had the sch3500 flip after 5 replacement phones for the same problem as<BR>"summertimejim"I made sprint eat it (take it back for a FULL refund) or I would have smashed that hunk of junk as well.<BR>Sprint will work for you IF YOU STAY on the <BR>major highways, but that's it!<P>****** If you let me beat the living crap out of your Sprint phone(s)<BR>I will give you 25% off any one in stock Fiero part till the end of January 2002!<P>One phone per person, per discount, per day.<BR>Don't forget to bring your camera.<P><BR>Man I loved smashing the crappy peice of <BR>sh t!<BR>Can I say crappy?<P>||||reg||12
Z||000022||artherd||12-27-2001||09:28 PM||||I've got a Samsung SCH-3500.    Love it!<P>The thing fits easily in my pocket, looks sexy, and I can make calls withought EVER pressing one button!<BR>(the voice recignition rocks.)<P>I've got the internet dialer adapter kit (works in MacOS 9 but not in OSX yet... Hey Lisa, think you can mention this to a certin someone over dinner?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> <P>Seriously, I drive all up and down the CA coast all the time (only about half the time for buisness, grin!) And I get great results from the phone. <P>Had it over a year now, still no problems.<P>Seems they've stoped making this phone now, hope mine stays working for a long time, I'm keeping it!<P><BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">      <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red.                     "Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver, In-Progreess.                                        -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
